## 4. Service Responsibilities

### What Services Should Do

**✅ Business Logic**:
- Encapsulate business rules
- Coordinate between multiple repositories
- Transform data
- Validate business rules

**✅ Orchestration**:
- Coordinate multiple operations
- Manage transactions
- Handle complex workflows
- Integrate with external services

**✅ Error Handling**:
- Catch and handle exceptions
- Log errors appropriately
- Transform exceptions to domain errors
- Provide meaningful error messages

### What Services Should NOT Do

**❌ HTTP Concerns**:
- Don't handle HTTP requests/responses
- Don't set HTTP status codes
- Don't handle routing
- Leave HTTP concerns to controllers

**❌ Data Access Details**:
- Don't directly access databases
- Don't write SQL queries
- Use repositories for data access
- Abstract data access

**❌ Presentation Logic**:
- Don't format data for display
- Don't handle UI concerns
- Return domain models or DTOs
- Let controllers handle presentation

