## 7. Error Handling Patterns

### Standardized Error Handling

**ExecuteOperationAsync Pattern**:

```csharp
protected async Task<T> ExecuteOperationAsync<T>(
    Func<Task<T>> operation, 
    string operationName)
{
    try
    {
        LogInformation("Starting operation", operationName);
        var result = await operation();
        LogInformation("Operation completed successfully", operationName);
        return result;
    }
    catch (Exception ex)
    {
        LogError(ex, operationName);
        throw; // Re-throw to allow caller to handle
    }
}
```

**Benefits**:
- Consistent error logging
- Operation tracking
- Error context preservation
- Re-throw for caller handling

### Custom Exception Handling

```csharp
public async Task<Vessel> GetVesselAsync(int vesselId)
{
    return await ExecuteOperationAsync(async () =>
    {
        var vessel = await _repository.GetByIdAsync(vesselId);
        
        if (vessel == null)
        {
            throw new KeyNotFoundException($"Vessel with ID {vesselId} not found");
        }
        
        return vessel;
    }, nameof(GetVesselAsync));
}
```

